  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Express $S=4+8+16+⋯+64+128$ in sigma notation.",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the terms of the corresponding sequence  \n\n$$\n4,\\,8,\\,16,\\,…,\\,64,\\,128.\n$$\n\n  \n\nare powers of $2,$ beginning with ${2}^{2}=4$ and ending with ${2}^{7}=128,$ so there are $6$ terms in total.  \n\nTherefore, the $n$th term of the sequence has the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={2}^{n+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ ranges from $n=1$ to $n=6.$ Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & ={2}^{1+1}=4 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={2}^{2+1}=8 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={2}^{3+1}=16 \\\\  & \\,\\,⋮ \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={2}^{5+1}=64 \\\\ {a}_{6} & ={2}^{6+1}=128\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nS=4+8+⋯+64+128={\\sum }_{n=1}^{6}{2}^{n+1}.\n$$",
